---

### 1. Framework Objectives
- Ensure AI systems remain reliable, safe, fair, and compliant after deployment
- Detect degradation (drift, hallucination, bias, performance drop) early
- Provide continuous, audit-ready evidence for Model Risk Management, auditors, and regulators
- Apply monitoring intensity proportional to risk
- Close the loop between production behavior and model improvement

---

### 2. Core Architecture: Five-Plane Observability Model

```
AI Applications / Agents
          │
          ▼
   ┌──────────────────┐
   │   Trace Store    │  ← Single source of truth
   └────────┬─────────┘
            │
   ┌────────┼────────────────────┐
   │        │         │          │
   ▼        ▼         ▼          ▼
Signal   Evaluation  Governance  Feedback
```

| Plane | Purpose | Key Outputs |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| **Trace** | Complete record of every AI interaction | Inputs, outputs, prompts, context, tool calls, versions, latency, cost, failures |
| **Signal** | Real-time operational health | Latency, errors, throughput, token cost, alerts |
| **Evaluation** | Continuous quality measurement | Faithfulness, hallucination, accuracy, fairness, drift scores |
| **Governance** | Control, policy & lifecycle | Inventory, risk tiers, approvals, change logs, retention |
| **Feedback** | Learning from reality | User ratings, corrections, incidents → improve models/prompts |

