### 3. Governance Structure for Monitoring & Evaluation

**Key Roles**
- **Use Case / Model Owner** — Business accountability for performance
- **AI Platform Team** — Owns Trace Store, observability tooling, LLM gateway
- **Model Risk Management (2nd Line)** — Independent challenge, validation, tiering
- **Compliance / Legal / Operational Risk** — Policy alignment and regulatory evidence
- **AI Governance Committee** — Senior oversight and exceptions
- **Internal Audit (3rd Line)** — Independent assurance

**Mandatory Controls**
- Every AI system must be registered in a central inventory before production
- Risk tier must be assigned (Critical / High / Medium / Low)
- Monitoring plan must be defined and approved according to tier
- Every material change requires re-evaluation and approval

---

### 4. Risk-Tiered Monitoring & Evaluation

| Risk Tier | Monitoring Frequency | Evaluation Depth | Change Control | Human Oversight |
|-----------|----------------------|------------------|----------------|-----------------|
| **Critical** | Continuous | Deep + continuous sampling | Formal + Independent validation | Mandatory review |
| **High** | Near real-time | Strong + frequent sampling | Formal approval | Sampling + escalation |
| **Medium** | Daily / Periodic | Standard | Standard approval | Spot checks |
| **Low** | Periodic | Lightweight | Lightweight | Minimal |

